1
00:00:03,300 --> 00:00:07,320
Open Interaction Center, Management, Voice Media.

2
00:00:07,320 --> 00:00:09,293
The library is empty.

3
00:00:09,293 --> 00:00:11,340
Click Add Voice Media.

4
00:00:14,033 --> 00:00:18,348
Enter a Name that people will recognize, such as Main hold music, and

5
00:00:18,348 --> 00:00:22,893
an optional Description that says which business or line the clip is for.

6
00:00:23,428 --> 00:00:27,952
Under Audio, choose an M.P.3, wave, O.G.G.

7
00:00:27,952 --> 00:00:32,288
or web M file of up to twenty megabytes.

8
00:00:32,754 --> 00:00:33,774
Click Save.

9
00:00:33,774 --> 00:00:38,094
The platform keeps the file as the clip's master copy, and sends a

10
00:00:38,094 --> 00:00:40,074
copy to the phone provider.

11
00:00:40,542 --> 00:00:44,212
The clip is listed with its format and a Master copy badge, and

12
00:00:44,212 --> 00:00:45,489
when it was saved.

13
00:00:45,489 --> 00:00:49,372
If the phone provider does not accept the upload, the clip is still

14
00:00:49,372 --> 00:00:52,352
saved with its master copy, and you see a warning.

